<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Pinterest Video Downloader Free - Save Pinterest Videos Online</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Pinterest video downloader free: paste a pin link and save the video as MP4. No signup, no app to install. Works on phone and computer." />
  <link rel="canonical" href="https://pinterest-video-downloader-tool.vercel.app/" />
  <meta name="google-site-verification" content="2oQ9nHqPWtFJt3BqpX0GzOX7KgKg7tO3nj1x7kJOhbs" />

  <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
  <meta property="og:title" content="Pinterest Video Downloader Free" />
  <meta property="og:description" content="Paste a Pinterest pin link and save the video as MP4. Free, no signup." />
  <meta property="og:url" content="https://pinterest-video-downloader-tool.vercel.app/" />

  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
</head>
<body>

  <header class="site-header">
    <nav class="navbar">
      <a href="/" class="nav-brand">Pinterest Video Downloader</a>
      <ul class="nav-links">
        <li><a href="#purpose">Purpose</a></li>
        <li><a href="#why">Why Use It</a></li>
        <li><a href="#format">What You Get</a></li>
        <li><a href="/how-to-download-pinterest-videos">Guide</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main>

    <!-- Hero / Tool -->
    <section class="hero" id="home">
      <div class="container">
        <h1>Pinterest Video Downloader Free</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">
          Use this pinterest video downloader free tool to save any Pinterest video.
          Paste the link, tap Get Video, and download it to your phone or computer.
        </p>

        <form action="/extract" method="POST" class="form">
          <div class="input-wrapper">
            <input
              type="text"
              id="pinUrlInput"
              name="pinUrl"
              placeholder="https://www.pinterest.com/pin/... or https://pin.it/..."
              value="<%= submittedUrl %>"
              required
            />
            <button type="button" class="clear-btn" onclick="clearInput()" title="Clear" aria-label="Clear">&times;</button>
          </div>
          <button type="submit">Get Video</button>
        </form>

        <% if (error) { %>
          <p class="error"><%= error %></p>
        <% } %>

        <% if (result) { %>
          <div class="result">
            <% if (result.thumbnail) { %>
              <img src="<%= result.thumbnail %>" alt="Pinterest video thumbnail" />
            <% } %>
            <% if (result.title) { %>
              <p class="title"><%= result.title %></p>
            <% } %>

            <button
              class="download-btn"
              data-url="<%= encodeURIComponent(result.videoUrl) %>"
              onclick="downloadVideo(this.dataset.url)"
            >
              Download Video
            </button>
            <p id="downloadStatus"></p>
          </div>
        <% } %>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="purpose">
      <h2>Why use a Pinterest video downloader free tool?</h2>
      <p>Pinterest has many useful videos, like recipes, DIY ideas and tutorials. But it has no button to download them. You can save a pin to a board, but the video only plays inside Pinterest. If the pin is deleted or you have no internet, you lose it.</p>
      <p>This tool fixes that. Copy the link of a video pin, paste it in the box above, and get the video as a file. You can keep it, watch it offline, or send it to another device.</p>

      <figure class="step-image">
        <img
          src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dc3lavmde/image/upload/v1791392335/inweb_gre33i.webp"
          alt="Pinterest video downloader free guide: Pinterest has no download button for videos"
          width="720"
          height="450"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>On Pinterest, there is no option to download the video. This tool solves that.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section id="devices">
      <h2>Works on any device</h2>
      <p>You use it in your browser, so there is nothing to install. It works on Android, iPhone, iPad, Windows, Mac and Linux.</p>
      <p>On a phone, the video usually goes to your Downloads folder or the Files app. On a computer, it goes to your browser's download folder. Chrome, Safari, Firefox and Edge all work.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="links">
      <h2>Which links can I use?</h2>
      <p>You can paste the full link from your browser, or the short pin.it link from the Share button in the Pinterest app. Short links work automatically.</p>
      <p>The link must be for a pin that has a video. Links to image pins, boards or profiles will not work.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="why">
      <h2>Why people use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>No account needed.</strong> No login, no signup and no email. Just paste a link.</li>
        <li><strong>We don't save your videos.</strong> The video goes straight to your device.</li>
        <li><strong>Free.</strong> No subscription and nothing to install.</li>
        <li><strong>Simple.</strong> Paste the link, tap one button, and the video is ready.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="format">
      <h2>What you get</h2>
      <p>You get the video as an MP4 file. MP4 plays on almost every phone, computer and TV. The quality is the same as the video on Pinterest. If the original is HD, your download is HD. If the original is low quality, the download will be too.</p>
      <p>Want help with each step? See our <a href="/how-to-download-pinterest-videos">step-by-step guide with pictures</a>.</p>
    </section>

    

  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <div class="container">
      <p>&copy; <%= new Date().getFullYear() %> Pinterest Video Downloader. All rights reserved.</p>
      <p>
        <a href="/how-to-download-pinterest-videos">Guide</a> 
      
      </p>
      <p class="footer-note">This is an independent tool and is not affiliated with Pinterest.</p>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <script>
    function clearInput() {
      var input = document.getElementById("pinUrlInput");
      input.value = "";
      input.focus();
    }

    async function downloadVideo(encodedUrl) {
      var status = document.getElementById("downloadStatus");
      status.textContent = "Downloading...";

      try {
        var response = await fetch("/download?url=" + encodedUrl);
        if (!response.ok) {
          throw new Error("Server returned status " + response.status);
        }

        var blob = await response.blob();
        if (blob.size === 0) {
          throw new Error("Received empty file");
        }

        var blobUrl = window.URL.createObjectURL(blob);
        var a = document.createElement("a");
        a.href = blobUrl;
        a.download = "pinterest-video.mp4";
        document.body.appendChild(a);
        a.click();
        a.remove();
        window.URL.revokeObjectURL(blobUrl);

        status.textContent = "Done!";
      } catch (err) {
        status.textContent = "Download failed. Please try again.";
      }
    }
  </script>
</body>
</html>